Bootstrap is a widely used open-source front-end framework originally developed by Twitter. It provides a set of CSS, JavaScript, and HTML components that make building responsive, mobile-first websites faster and easier.

🔑 Key Features
Responsive Grid System: Built on a 12-column layout for flexible design.

Predefined CSS Classes: For typography, buttons, forms, tables, and navigation.

Reusable Components: Modals, dropdowns, carousels, alerts, badges, progress bars.

JavaScript Plugins: Tooltips, popovers, collapsible menus, carousels.

Customization: Modify via Sass variables or override styles.

Cross-browser Compatibility: Works consistently across modern browsers.

⚡ Advantages
Rapid development with minimal custom CSS.

Consistent design language across projects.

Strong community support and documentation.

Easy integration with frameworks like Angular, React, and ASP.NET MVC.

🎯 20 Bootstrap Interview Questions & Answers
Basics
What is Bootstrap?  
A front-end framework providing pre-styled components and a responsive grid system to speed up web development.

Why is Bootstrap mobile-first?  
It designs for small screens first, then scales up for larger devices.

Explain the Bootstrap Grid System.  
A 12-column layout with classes like .col-sm-6, .col-md-4 for responsive design.

Difference between Bootstrap 4 and Bootstrap 5?  
Bootstrap 5 removed jQuery, added enhanced grid system, utilities API, and improved forms.

What are breakpoints in Bootstrap?  
Predefined screen sizes (sm, md, lg, xl, xxl) controlling responsive behavior.

Components
How do you create a responsive navbar?  
Use .navbar, .navbar-expand-lg, .navbar-light/dark with .collapse for toggling.

Purpose of the .container class?  
Centers content with responsive padding. Variants: .container-fluid (full width).

Explain Bootstrap buttons.  
Classes like .btn, .btn-primary, .btn-outline-success provide consistent styles.

How do you implement a modal?  
Use .modal, .modal-dialog, .modal-content. Trigger via data-bs-toggle="modal".

What is a Jumbotron?  
A large block for showcasing info (deprecated in Bootstrap 5, replaced by utilities).

Utilities & Customization
What are utility classes?  
Predefined classes for spacing (.m-3), text alignment (.text-center), display (.d-flex).

How do you override Bootstrap styles?  
Write custom CSS after Bootstrap’s stylesheet or use Sass variables.

Difference between .d-none and .invisible?  
.d-none removes element from layout; .invisible hides but keeps space reserved.

How do you align items using Flexbox utilities?  
Classes like .d-flex, .justify-content-center, .align-items-start.

Difference between .container and .container-fluid?  
.container has fixed width at breakpoints; .container-fluid spans full width.

Advanced
How do you create a responsive table?  
Wrap table in .table-responsive for horizontal scrolling on small devices.

Explain form validation classes.  
.is-valid, .is-invalid provide instant feedback styling for inputs.

Role of Bootstrap’s JavaScript plugins?  
Add interactivity (modals, tooltips, carousels) using vanilla JS in Bootstrap 5.

How do you use Bootstrap with React or Angular?  
Import Bootstrap CSS/JS or use libraries like react-bootstrap and ng-bootstrap.

What are Bootstrap Icons?  
A separate icon library introduced in Bootstrap 5 with scalable vector icons.
